WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.587
"The Best Supplement to Prevent Skin Cancer"

00:00:07.051 --> 00:00:09.946
Nicotinamide,
also known as niacinamide,

00:00:09.946 --> 00:00:11.820
is a form of vitamin B3

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.920
that has been used topically
for decades

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.500
in the cosmetic field
to prevent skin aging,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.460
as I've already covered.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.880
So, researchers decided
to put it to the test orally

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.740
for skin cancer prevention.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.120
In a petri dish,

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.040
skin samples taken
from breast reduction

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.300
and tummy tuck surgeries

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.880
exposed to UV
with or without niacinamide

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.580
found that it enhanced
DNA repair.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.760
Would this translate out
into less cancer?

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.760
In a Phase II trial,
dozens of individuals

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.520
with four or more
precancerous actinic keratoses

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.440
each were randomized
to take a placebo

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.380
or 500 mg of niacinamide
once or twice a day.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.620
Within two months,
there was a 35 percent reduction

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.440
in actinic keratoses
in the twice-a-day group,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.700
and a 15 percent reduction

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.620
in the once-a-day group
compared to placebo.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.220
It's not that they developed
fewer in those months,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.800
but more
spontaneously disappeared

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.060
in the niacinamide groups.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.400
What about actual cancers?

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.940
By month four, there were
five times fewer cancers

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.420
(11 placebo participants
developed 20 new skin cancers

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.400
versus only two
niacinamide participants

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.260
developing a total
of four new cancers).

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.740
Normally, it would be difficult
to fund studies

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.860
on nonpatentable products that
only cost a few cents a day,

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.860
but the results of this
and a similar study

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.360
on organ transplant patients

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.660
were so extraordinary
ONTRAC was born.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:34.440
Oral Nicotinamide
to Reduce Actinic Cancer

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.780
was a publicly-funded
phase III trial

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.640
randomizing hundreds of people

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.320
with a personal history
of skin cancers

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.020
(actinic means UV-induced)

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.960
to 500 mg of nicotinamide
twice daily

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.060
or placebo for a full year.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:52.560
By the end, there were
25 percent fewer cancers

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.840
with no significant
side effects

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.280
for just pennies a day.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.260
You have to keep it up, though.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.840
At a six-month follow-up
after the study was over,

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.620
the cancer rates equalized back
to baseline rates.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.600
What are the downsides?

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.700
A study of 500 people

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.580
put on up to three grams
of niacinamide a day

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.920
for five years (trying
to prevent type 1 diabetes)

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.560
unearthed no adverse effects
over placebo

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.440
(though it failed to prevent
type 1 diabetes).

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.200
The high tolerance
of niacinamide

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.720
is partly due
to its water-soluble nature,

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.940
such that you just pee out
any excess.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:30.480
But those with end-stage
kidney failure on dialysis

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.250
don't have functioning kidneys,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.260
and so, blood levels
should be monitored,

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.080
as, in that context,
niacinamide can cause

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.900
a serious, though reversible,
drop in platelets,

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.460
which are important
for blood clotting.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.120
High enough doses may become
toxic to the liver, though,

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.860
even with normal kidneys.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.220
Vasodilatory side effects,
like facial flushing,

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.620
attributed to niacinamide
in some older studies

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:55.680
were likely due
to a less purified form

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.320
contaminated with
residual niacin.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.360
(I know it's confusing!

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.820
Niacin, also known
as nicotinic acid,

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.640
is the precursor of,
but very different from,

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:08.580
niacinamide, which is
synonymous with nicotinamide.)

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:11.580
One concern
regarding any treatment

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.560
for a largely lifestyle disease

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.560
is that individuals may neglect
other defensive measures,

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.960
overconfident in
the supplement's protection.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.680
Regarding drug interactions,
a concern has been raised

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.620
about taking niacinamide
together with carbamazepine,

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:28.740
a popular anti-seizure drug
(sold as Tegretol).

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:29.760
But, in general,

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.040
as the ONTRAC researchers
concluded,

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.440
"Oral nicotinamide
is safe and effective

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.440
in reducing the rates
of new nonmelanoma skin cancers

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.900
and precancerous growths
in high-risk patients."

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.220
To their credit, a 2021 survey
of skin cancer surgeons found

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.560
that three-quarters
recommended its use.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:51.300
Other than nicotinamide,
how else might we protect

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.340
against skin cancer
from the inside out?

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:56.100
That's what I'll cover next.

